Declares a helper function that generates an anti-aliased circular image to prevent jagged edges on screen.
Line 31 (scale = 4): Sets a supersampling multiplier of 4.
Line 32 (large_size = size * scale): Calculates oversized dimensions. If size is 110px, large_size becomes 440px.
Line 33 (img = Image.new("RGBA", (large_size, large_size), (0, 0, 0, 0))): Creates a blank transparent RGBA image canvas at 440x440 resolution.
Line 34 (draw = ImageDraw.Draw(img)): Binds a drawing tool to the canvas.
Line 35 (draw.ellipse([(0, 0), (large_size - 1, large_size - 1)], fill=bg_color)): Draws a solid circle filling the 440x440 box with bg_color.
Line 36 (return img.resize((size, size), Image.Resampling.LANCZOS)): Downscales the 440x440 circle back down to 110x110 using Lanczos resampling. This mathematically averages pixel colors along edges to smooth jagged edges.
